FKg6SKx"}]},{"role":"tool","sequence":15,"content":[{"type":"toolResult","text":"{\"approval_id\":\"appr_6\",\"total_cost_usd_micros\":1760000,\"max_cost_usd_micros\":1760000,\"next\":\"Present this plan to the user and wait for their reply. Do not execute until they approve.\"}","toolCallId":"toolu_01WAh4eNr4mZ3P9vgFKg6SKx","toolName":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_prepare_route","isError":false}]},{"role":"assistant","sequence":16,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan is ready (`appr_6`). Nothing has been executed, and I'm waiting for your approval.\n\n**Route: bridge ETH to Base, then swap to USDC on Base**\n\n| # | Leg | Quote | In | Expected out | Cost | Delay |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `eth-bridge-eth-base` (eth1 → base1) | `q_2` | 0.1 ETH (100000000000000000 wei) | 0.099833333333333333 ETH | $1.40 | ~60 s |\n| 2 | `base-swap-eth-usdc` (base1) | `q_5` | 99793333333333333 wei ETH | 299.079999 USDC (299079999 base units) | $0.36 | ~2 s |\n\n- **Cost:** total $1.76, max $1.76. The policy cap is $8.00. Slippage cap is 50 bps, deadline is 1800 s, and quotes expire after 300 s.\n- **Cheaper than the alternative:** swapping on Ethereum and then bridging USDC (`q_1` + `q_3`) costs $5.30 and delivers 296.5 USDC. It would also leave base1 holding USDC with 0 ETH for gas.\n- **Gas reserve on base1:** it has 0 ETH now, so I keep about 0.00004 ETH (2× `gas_per_tx`) unswapped. One share covers the swap's own gas and the other covers one later transaction. This costs about $0.06 of USDC.\n- **Gas reserve on eth1:** it keeps about 0.05 ETH after the bridge.\n- **Execution:** I'll submit one leg at a time and read the base1 balance after each confirms. If the bridged ETH differs from the quote, I'll re-quote leg 2 before submitting it. If either leg falls short of its quoted output by more than 50 bps, I'll halt.\n\nApprove to proceed, refuse, or set a different cost cap."}]},{"role":"user","sequence":17,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, go ahead with that plan.